 "intro": "Near Canusium in Apulia, 209 BC. You are Marcus Claudius Marcellus, the 'Sword of Rome', consul for the fifth time, following Hannibal.",
 "debrief": "In Livy’s account, the first day went badly and the Roman right gave way. That night Marcellus shamed his men, who begged to fight again. On the second day they fought hard; a wounded elephant turned and trampled the Carthaginian lines, and Hannibal fell back. Roman losses were heavy, and Marcellus rested at Venusia. He was killed in an ambush the next year. Some historians doubt parts of Livy’s account. The other choices are what-ifs.",
